      "source": [
        "from IPython import display\n",
        "import time\n",
        "\n",
        "# Assuming ds is defined elsewhere\n",
        "nt = len(ds.time)\n",
        "eq = ds.sel(lat=0, method='nearest')\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(15,6))\n",
        "\n",
        "for j in np.arange(nt):\n",
        "    plt.clf() # Clear the figure\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Select data for the current time step\n",
        "    eq.sl.isel(time=j).plot(color='IndianRed', linewidth=4)\n",
        "\n",
        "    date_str = eq.time.isel(time=j).dt.strftime('%d-%b-%Y').values\n",
        "\n",
        "    plt.title(f'Sea Level on {date_str}')\n",
        "    # lock the x and y axis so its not twitchy\n",
        "    plt.ylim(-0.3, 0.3)\n",
        "    plt.xlim(eq.lon.min(), eq.lon.max())\n",
        "\n",
        "    plt.grid(True)\n",
        "    # animation code\n",
        "    display.display(plt.gcf())\n",
        "    display.clear_output(wait=True)\n",
        "    time.sleep(0.1)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "RApbUVx_F260"
      },
      "source": [
        "A note on data processing:\n",
        "\n",
        "In order to correct MATLAB's proprietary datetime, I had to go onto MATLAB and create a .m script that changed the date to a string. .mat files are sometimes used to exchange data amongst professionals in the field. So in case you ever run into this problem again in your careers, I am attaching the code I used to fix this\n",
        "```\n",
        "% 1. Load the data\n",
        "load('Module2_large.mat');\n",
        "\n",
        "% 2. Extract and convert to a cell array of strings\n",
        "% (Cell arrays of strings are often more \"stable\" for Scipy than the modern string class)\n",
        "alt_time_str = cellstr(string(ALT.t, 'yyyy-MM-dd'));\n",
        "\n",
        "% 3. Extract the numeric data\n",
        "sl  = ALT.sl;\n",
        "lat = ALT.lat;\n",
        "lon = ALT.lon;\n",
        "oni = ONI;\n",
        "\n",
        "% 4. Save using the -v7 flag for maximum Scipy compatibility\n",
        "save('Module2_Python_Ready.mat', 'sl', 'lat', 'lon', 'alt_time_str', 'oni', '-v7');\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "id": "RApbUVx_F260"
    },
